Heya :D I'm Anahita &mdash; a fourth-year computer science student at UBC. I'm a
big fan of programming languages and type theory. I also really like 
functional programming.

I'm currently an undergraduate teaching assistant at UBC for CPSC 210 (Software 
Construction) and a undergraduate research assistant with the 
[ARLI](https://williamjbowman.com/arli/index.html) research group in the
[Software Practices Lab](https://spl.cs.ubc.ca/) working on a dependent type 
preserving compiler framework based on 
[Logical Frameworks](https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/logical+framework).

Outside of my education, I enjoy reading, (song)writing, running, and hiking.

I hope you enjoy the website :)
